egl,zink: add an ohos platform for zink

OpenHarmony's EGL wrapper loads a vendor EGL and GLES. This EGL platform
makes Zink that EGL. Window surfaces use kopper with VK_OHOS_surface,
which OpenHarmony's Vulkan swapchain layer provides. The layer takes the
NativeWindow's buffers and hands them to the Vulkan driver with
VK_OHOS_native_buffer. Swaps go through kopper, with damage and buffer
age.

The swapchain layer has no BGRA formats, so the window configs are RGBA.
Mesa makes RGBA configs only when the loader reports
DRI_LOADER_CAP_RGBA_ORDERING, and it asked only the image loader, which
a kopper platform doesn't have. Version 2 of the kopper loader extension
adds getCapability, and the platform reports RGBA ordering through it.

render_service imports the buffers of other surfaces with
eglCreateImageKHR(EGL_NATIVE_BUFFER_OHOS) and a NativeWindowBuffer. The
platform imports the buffer's dma-buf as a linear image with the
handle's row pitch, because a BufferHandle describes no tiling.
render_service passes its context with this target, so the platform
ignores the context. The value of EGL_NATIVE_BUFFER_OHOS comes from
OpenHarmony's EGL headers.

The surface and kopper code is a port of OpenHarmony's Mesa,
https://gitee.com/openharmony/third_party_mesa3d at
ea74a6339917390657db153cb9792f9ccac9f5ae, which is MIT-licensed like
Mesa. The image import, the configs for each NativeBuffer format and
the swap interval are new.

